  "beforeSUTFreezeSHA256": "c67e65e32dc253834b9ee88618552c80c887e3406e914d80a1a2d605fd625aaa",
  "causalFinding": "All five actual constructors exhaust2Mcharged operations, at classifier source IDs6:5/6:6/8:2/8:0/11:0, while recorded storage peaks are below100k. The source scans every original facet of each possible owner on every occupancy ray attempt, including facets wholly behind the origin on a ray coordinate. Existing facet boxes/tree can exclude those impossible hits. Raw traces have no inner-stage work split: no measured dominance, eventual completion or full-storage-fit claim.",
  "correction": [
    "A conservative ray-box predicate rejects only a strict forward-axis separation. Positive direction rejects box.upper<origin; negative rejects box.lower>origin; zero direction rejects origin strictly outside the closed interval. Equality remains eligible. Comparisons use existing exact coordinates; no new rational arithmetic, precision guard or approximate ray computation.",
    "Reuse the existing retained facet tree. Prune a node only when its closed box misses the owner box or fails the necessary ray predicate; visit left before right, test eligible leaf facets and filter the exact owner ID. Output ordinals retain the original source order, without assuming owner contiguity.",
    "Extract the unchanged exact plane/hit/contains parity loop into one helper shared by flat/indexed visits. Keep zero/negative-hit exclusion, coplanar-origin ambiguity, edge ambiguity, parity, normal-facing direction and retry sequence. Every returned candidate uses that full original test.",
    "Owners with at most4existing8-facet leaves keep the original flat scan to avoid small-query overhead. Cache one facet-count record per owner: reserve11members/owner instead of10 and add one charged count update per original facet, keeping all six prior coordinate charges. The execution choice never changes geometric eligibility.",
    "Charge every visited node, owner-box meet, forward-axis comparison, leaf visit and exact candidate test. Admit up toNreturned ordinals plus the existing stack bound in scopes, releasing on success/error. No saved work is credited unless the corresponding traversal or full ray test is actually omitted."
  ],
  "soundnessProof": [
    "If a forward ray hits a facet at t>=0, every coordinate hit is in that facet box and on the signed half-line from the origin. Thus no axis can satisfy the strict rejection. Every ancestor contains the facet box, so ancestor rejection is also impossible.",
    "For the denominator-zero coplanar ambiguity, contains(origin) implies origin lies inside the facet box. It cannot be rejected for any signed or zero direction. All equality contacts remain candidates.",
    "A node containing an owner facet necessarily overlaps that owner union box. Left-first contiguous traversal and the owner ID filter return the same order as the full scan after removing impossible facets. Therefore all ambiguity/retry decisions and parity contributions remain unchanged."
  ],
  "newTests": [
    "Independent corner-based necessary predicate matches exact ordered candidates across interleaved owners, positive/negative/zero-axis directions and boundary origins. Flat and indexed exact parity/ambiguity match. Cached owner counts, one-short query scratch refusal, admitted peak and release are checked.",
    "Complete independent3xsubdivided cube108facets and buried120-source case, analytic volume64/output108facets. Compare ordered Facets, every witness source/cells/physical/protected/output/stars/area field and both public witness verifications. Require lower complete charged work on both large-owner cases; record all peaks/retained counters.",
    "All original six controls, adverse small-work observations, tests/assertions and frozen references retained unchanged. Small owners incur the explicit new count bookkeeping; no claim of universal savings."
  ],
